window.EN={"1":"Having overcome numerous obstacles, Leif's army has reached Munster.","2":"As if to bar their way, the castle of Munster towers high above them.","3":"Into that \"Demon King's Castle,\" from which they once fled, Leif and his army set foot once more.","4":"To take back what was lost... To carve open a new age...","5":"Raydrik, I hear you have let the rebels get in as far as the castle.","6":"Sir... But if you will grant me just a little more time, I will drive them from this castle without fail...","7":"Do not speak of what you cannot do. It is plain to anyone that the rebels have the overwhelming advantage...","8":"......","9":"I had thought you would be a little more useful, but so this is all... Our association ends here.","10":"Please wait, Bishop Veld! If you abandon us, we...","11":"Then do something about it. As a parting gift at least, I will lend you a detachment of the Berg Rosen.","12":"Prince, don't let your guard down. Raydrik has almost no soldiers left, but mercenaries lie in wait inside the palace.","13":"Among them, a swordsman named Galzus is dangerous. Face him head-on and you have no chance of winning.","14":"Galzus... Then... what should we do?","15":"All we can do is lure him in skillfully and bring him down with my Forseti, but even then I can't say whether he can be beaten.","16":"We have too few soldiers here. August, why did you divide the soldiers into three places?","17":"One unit is to take back the children; one unit is to seize the Loptr priests.","18":"Both are a race against time, so I had them go in separately.","19":"I understand rescuing the children, but what's this about Loptr priests?","20":"In the eastern corner there is a Loptr chapel, and many priests are stationed there.","21":"They use Berserk and Sleep staves, so it is dangerous to leave them be.","22":"I see... But then you mean for us alone to fight Raydrik?","23":"Indeed. There is no leeway for the others to join us.","24":"Prince Leif, it is certainly a hard fight, but it can't be helped.","25":"I'll do something about the enemy in front. You think only of defeating Raydrik!","26":"Yes! I will defeat Raydrik without fail!","27":"Prince, do not let your guard down. Raydrik has almost no soldiers left,","28":"but mercenaries lie in wait inside the palace. In particular, you must not engage the swordsman named Galzus.","29":"Galzus... Then... what should we do?","30":"I cannot say anything for certain, but if the girl named Mareeta is with you, something may be done.","31":"Galzus seems to have some deep connection with that girl.","32":"Mareeta... August! Why did you divide the soldiers into three places?","33":"One unit is to take back the children; one unit is to seize the Loptr priests.","34":"Both are a race against time, so I had them go in separately.","35":"I understand rescuing the children, but what's this about Loptr priests?","36":"In the eastern corner there is a Loptr chapel, and many priests are stationed there.","37":"They use Berserk and Sleep staves, so it is dangerous to leave them be.","38":"I see... But then you mean for us alone to fight Raydrik?","39":"Indeed. There is no leeway for the others to join us.","40":"Prince Leif, it is certainly a hard fight, but it cannot be helped.","41":"I, too, will do all I can. Prince, please think only of defeating Raydrik!","42":"Yes! I will defeat Raydrik without fail, you'll see!","43":"Prince, do not let your guard down. Raydrik has almost no soldiers left,","44":"but mercenaries lie in wait inside the palace. Among them, against the swordsman named Galzus you have no chance of winning.","45":"Galzus... Then what do you say we should do, August?","46":"There is likely nothing for it but to lure him in and bury him in one stroke. Even then I cannot say whether he can be beaten...","47":"We have too few soldiers here. August, why did you divide the soldiers into three places?","48":"One unit is to take back the children; one unit is to seize the Loptr priests.","49":"Both are a race against time, so I had them go in separately.","50":"I understand rescuing the children, but what's this about Loptr priests?","51":"In the eastern corner there is a Loptr chapel, and many priests are stationed there.","52":"They use Berserk and Sleep staves, so it is dangerous to leave them be.","53":"I see... But then you mean for us alone to fight Raydrik?","54":"Indeed. There is no leeway for the others to join us.","55":"Prince Leif, it is certainly a hard fight, but now that it has come to this, we can only ask you to do your utmost, Lord Leif!","56":"I know. I will defeat Raydrik without fail, you'll see!!","57":"Prince, do not let your guard down.","58":"Raydrik has almost no soldiers left, but mercenaries lie in wait inside the palace.","59":"August, why did you divide the soldiers into three places?","60":"One unit is to take back the children; one unit is to seize the Loptr priests.","61":"Both are a race against time, so I had them go in separately.","62":"I understand rescuing the children, but what's this about Loptr priests?","63":"In the eastern corner there is a Loptr chapel, and many priests are stationed there.","64":"They use Berserk and Sleep staves, so it is dangerous to leave them be.","65":"I see... But then you mean for us alone to fight Raydrik?","66":"Indeed. There is no leeway for the others to join us.","67":"Prince Leif, it is certainly a hard fight, but now that it has come to this, we can only ask you to do your utmost, Lord Leif!","68":"I know. I will defeat Raydrik without fail, you'll see!!","69":"Huh? I've come somewhere strange. What's this door?","70":"Whoa, it looks kind of scary... Hey, everyone, wait for meee!","71":"You are... the swordsman who rescued me... I've wanted to meet you all this time.","72":"Why did you come back? You're a woman, and still a child at that. A sword is not a toy.","73":"Back then... bewitched by the cursed sword, I met my father in a dream.","74":"I was still small when I was separated from my father, but even so I remember clearly.","75":"My father was big, and strong, and a kind man.","76":"Swordsman Galzus... you... are my father, aren't you!","77":"!...","78":"Why won't you say anything! Please! Tell me it's so!!","79":"Don't you... resent me...?","80":"Resent you? Never...","81":"I was caught by the slave traders because I didn't do as you told me, Father.","82":"Besides, right after that, Lady Eyvel saved me.","83":"I have never resented you, Father, not even once!","84":"I'm sorry. I kept searching all this time, but I couldn't find you...","85":"And I am now utterly stained with people's blood. I thought it better to have nothing more to do with you.","86":"No!... Whatever may happen, I am your daughter, Father...","87":"...... The one who saved you and raised you is that swordswoman who was turned to stone?","88":"Yes...","89":"......","90":"Then I cannot leave it be. As an Isaachian of sorts myself, I always repay a debt I owe!","91":"It was a severe battle, but it seems the palace has largely been secured. The way you fought was splendid too, Prince.","92":"But August, was Raydrik really defeated?","93":"I'm sure I dealt the finishing blow, but his form vanished like an illusion.","94":"This castle seems to be shrouded in some evil power.","95":"A secret temple of the Loptr Church has been built beneath Munster Castle, so that may be the cause.","96":"Unless that is destroyed, it cannot be said that liberation has truly been achieved.","97":"A secret temple... Loptr's stronghold in Thracia.","98":"Yes. The one in charge of it is Bishop Veld, Manfroy's confidant.","99":"Bishop Veld... What kind of man is he?","100":"As the one responsible for the Thracian diocese, he directed everything.","101":"Pushing forward the child hunts, having the Berg Rosen burn villages: it was all his doing.","102":"The likes of Raydrik are nothing more than errand boys.","103":"According to the prisoners, it was also Veld who turned Lady Eyvel to stone.","104":"Wh-what! I won't forgive him!... That man, Veld!...","105":"August! Do we know where the temple is?","106":"Yes. We have already located it.","107":"However, Bishop Veld is holed up there with numerous mage soldiers, so taking it will not be easy.","108":"We could also wait until Lord Seliph's army arrives, but in that case there is a risk of letting Veld escape.","109":"The tragedy he brought to Thracia is beyond anything Raydrik did.","110":"We cannot let Veld escape! Isn't that right, August!!","111":"But... rescuing Eyvel comes first now. August, what should we do!","112":"We have obtained the Kia Staff,","113":"but as I said before, only those of Manfroy's bloodline can use this staff.","114":"Regrettably, there is nothing we can do at present...","115":"So it's no use after all! We can't save Eyvel!!","116":"Ahh... What on earth was it all for!...","117":"That's not true. I can use that staff.","118":"Sara!?... You?... Is that true!!","119":"Yes, I can use it. I can tell. That seal... it's Grandfather's.","120":"Grandfather...? It can't be... Sara, are you Manfroy's granddaughter!?","121":"I don't want to talk about Grandfather. I hate him. What does it matter?","122":"Come on, let's go, Lord Leif. Don't forget the Kia Staff!","123":"Hmph. You say you've come to defeat me!?","124":"Fools! You are the ones who will die!!","125":"Ugh... Absurd... Why has it come to this...","126":"Bishop Veld... please... I don't want to die yet...","127":"...Save... me... gwah...","128":"Pitiful. Curse your own fate...","129":"Kh... Mareeta... I...","130":"Heh... How far I've fallen, to be shown mercy by an enemy..."};
